================================================================
INFRASTRUCTURE LESSON: THE bd-DB CONTENTION CEILING
================================================================

The dominant operational finding of this phase. The .beads/beads.db
SQLite store (now 3193 issues) does NOT sustain 7 concurrent panes each
running br + the pre-commit `bd sync --flush-only`.

Failure modes observed + recovered:
  1. BUILD STORM (early): 39 concurrent local cargo checks, load 10.83.
     Recovered by nudging all panes to light-verify (rustfmt + git
     diff --check + ONE targeted cargo check --lib), citing the RCH-E327
     fallback bd-17c65.10.17.1.2. Throughput restored.
  2. ZOMBIE CARGO CHECKS: an 84-minute + a 1-hour cargo check held the
     build lock, silently blocking bd-26jks for ~12 ticks. Killed per
     the ETIME>1h rule.
  3. bd-SYNC LIVELOCK (acute): 5 concurrent `bd sync --flush-only`
     thrashing the SQLite write lock, load spiked 19→31, zero commits
     for 16 min, the oldest sync stuck 13 min. Killed the livelocked
     syncs (recoverable — beads.db is source-of-truth, JSONL regenerates;
     verified 3193 valid lines post-kill, zero data loss). Lifted with a
     SERIALIZED-COMMIT rule (check .git/index.lock + pgrep bd sync before
     committing) → contention dropped 5→1 sync, br responsive again.

Takeaway for the next session: this DB sustains ~1-2 concurrent
committers, not 7. The remaining long-tail (below) should be drained by
a FOCUSED 2-3 pane session, OR by sharding the bead DB per-domain, NOT
by another 7-way swarm.

